<%# 
Cistergraphia Input Form
=======================

Purpose:
- Provides user interface for message input
- Simple, focused single-purpose form

Design Decisions:
- Minimal form fields
- Clear labeling
- Required field validation
- Consistent styling with layout

Constraints:
- Message field plus an optional passphrase (secret mode)
- Must validate non-empty input
- Posts to /generate endpoint
- Links to the /decode form
%>
<form method="post" action="/generate">
  <label for="message">Enter your message:</label><br>
  <input type="text" id="message" name="message" maxlength="500" required><br>
  <label for="passphrase">Passphrase (optional, at least 8 characters):</label><br>
  <input type="password" id="passphrase" name="passphrase" minlength="8" autocomplete="new-password"><br>
  <p class="hint">
    Without a passphrase you get the <strong>game</strong>: a classic cipher anyone can crack with a bit of work.
    With one you get <strong>secret mode</strong>: the message is encrypted (AES-256-GCM) and only that passphrase can reveal it.
  </p>
  <input type="submit" value="Generate">
</form>
<p>Received a Cistergraphia? <a href="/decode">Decode it</a>.</p> 